 class=\"hl\">nothing like as good as</span> I expected it to be."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"It&rsquo;s <span class=\"hl\">really not worth</span> seeing."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"note","title":"Как это работает","html":"It&rsquo;s <span class=\"hl\">much more</span> interesting <span class=\"hl\">than</span> the first one."},{"stage":"Grammar","type":"choice","title":"","prompt":"Which one is the strongest way of saying something was bad?","options":["the first","the second","the third","the fourth"],"answer":"the fourth"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Normal or extreme? Choose the adverb that goes with the adjective.","prompt":"The ending was ____ brilliant.","options":["a bit","very","absolutely"],"answer":"absolutely"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Normal or extreme? Choose the adverb that goes with the adjective.","prompt":"The middle hour was ____ disappointing.","options":["quite","very much","absolutely"],"answer":"quite"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Normal or extreme? Choose the adverb that goes with the adjective.","prompt":"The special effects are ____ astonishing.","options":["absolutely","very","a bit"],"answer":"absolutely"},{"stage":"Practice","type":"choice","title":"Normal or extreme? Choose the adverb that goes with the adjective.","prompt":"The cinema was ____ cold.","options":["very much","absolutely","very"],"answer":"very"},{"stage":"Speaking","type":"write","title":"Check your own review. Which of them did you do?","sub":"Напиши ответ, затем проверь себя","placeholder":"Твой ответ…","model":"Comparing: much more… than · nothing like as… as · the most… I’ve ever… · compared with…"},{"stage":"Wrap","type":"checklist","title":"Отметь, чему научился","sub":"Я могу…","items":["✓ judge a film strongly — dreadful, disappointing, astonishing, brilliant, infuriating","✓ put incredibly with normal adjectives and absolutely with extreme ones","✓ compare two things — much more… than, nothing like as… as, compared with","✓ recommend something — It’s worth…ing, I’d highly recommend…","✓ turn something down politely, three different ways","✓ write a review with a claim, a criticism, a comparison and a verdict"]}]}